### Manual API smoke tests (VS Code "REST Client"). Put real values in your own copy — never commit credentials.

### Health (public, reveals nothing)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/health/ready

### Create the FIRST superAdmin — preferred: `npm run create-superadmin` (no HTTP endpoint needed).
### This endpoint 404s unless BOOTSTRAP_SECRET is set on the server and works only while no superAdmin exists.
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/superadmin
Content-Type: application/json
X-Bootstrap-Secret: <BOOTSTRAP_SECRET from backend/.env>

{
  "name": "Your Name",
  "email": "you@example.com",
  "password": "<choose-a-strong-password>"
}

### Login
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "you@example.com", "password": "<your-password>" }
